<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  BlackstarCompany.xml                    Jawa_Patches · authored 2026-08-14
  ============================================================================

  Builds FACTION_SPEC.md section 10, "Blackstar Company ; PATCH vanilla
  `Pirate`". A reskin, not a new def.

  READ FROM THE SHIPPED DEF, 2026-08-14 ; not inferred:
  C:\Program Files (x86)\Steam\steamapps\common\RimWorld\Data\Core\Defs\
    FactionDefs\Factions_Misc.xml

      Name                        PirateBandBase   (it is its own abstract root)
      ParentName                  FactionBase
      label                       pirate gang
      pawnSingular / pawnsPlural  pirate / pirates
      leaderTitle                 boss
      settlementGenerationWeight  1
      permanentEnemy              true             PRESENT on the def itself
      factionNameMaker            NamerFactionPirate
      techLevel                   Spacer
      pawnGroupMakers             6 Combat groups + 1 Settlement

  ⭐ Unlike `OutlanderCivil` and `TribeCivil`, this def carries every field the
  spec touches ON ITSELF ; `FactionBase` supplies only the loot curve and a
  message string. So all six operations are `Replace`, and none of them is an
  `Add`.

  🔴 `permanentEnemy` STAYS true. R12 amends pillar 5 rather than patching this
  false, because the vanilla raid economy is built on the pirate faction being
  permanently hostile and turning it off guts it. The dossier's "No" is fiction,
  not an engine instruction. No operation touches the field.

  ⛔ `factionNameMaker`, `settlementNameMaker` and the raid curves are untouched.
  They are inherited or shipped and already balanced.

  🔴 `pawnGroupMakers` IS NOW SURGERY TOO - "R15's group surgery is the Empire's
  alone" is SUPERSEDED, 2026-08-22, by DECIDE's ruling in
  `design/Jawa/worldbuilding/pawnkind_roster.md`, "Every authored kind must be
  FIELDED", carried as `AUTHORED_KINDS_MUST_FIELD_1`. All four
  `Jawa_Blackstar_*` kinds existed and NO FactionDef fielded any of them; this
  file saying the groups were untouched is exactly why nobody noticed. Measured:
  `grep -rn Jawa_Blackstar_ src/` returned only their own definitions.

  ⇒ The six COMBAT groups have their `options` replaced; `Settlement` is left
  vanilla on purpose, and so are Trader and Peaceful wherever they exist. The
  48-kind roster has no trader or civilian role to put in them, and a faction
  that cannot send a caravan or defend its own settlement is a worse defect than
  the one being fixed.
  ⚠️ The LEADER does not go in a group maker. A leader is generated once per
  faction, so `Jawa_Blackstar_Leader` goes to `fixedLeaderKinds` - an ADD, since
  no vanilla FactionDef in `Factions_Misc.xml` writes that field. This is the
  same mechanism that has been quietly fielding `Jawa_Empire_Leader` all along,
  and the reason reporting it as "orphaned" was a false positive.

  ⚠️ The ideo layer (`fixedIdeo` / `ideoName` "the Contract", deliberately with
  NO Raider meme) is NOT in this file. It lands in `FactionReligions.xml` in its
  own pass, the same way the Empire's did.

  SAFETY
  ======
  Everything sits inside a conditional on the def existing, so the file is a
  silent no-op rather than a wall of red if the vessel ever moves. Every
  defName written here is vanilla Core, so no `MayRequire` is owed.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Patch>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="Pirate"]</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationSequence">
      <operations>

        <!-- "pirate gang" -> the campaign name. -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="Pirate"]/label</xpath>
          <value><label>Blackstar Company</label></value>
        </li>

        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="Pirate"]/description</xpath>
          <value>
            <description>Not a faction so much as one dangerous person with a name who is coming for you.\n\nIndependent hunters bound by a professional code, taking contracts rather than pillaging. The distinction matters to them. It will not matter to you when they arrive.</description>
          </value>
        </li>

        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="Pirate"]/pawnSingular</xpath>
          <value><pawnSingular>hunter</pawnSingular></value>
        </li>

        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="Pirate"]/pawnsPlural</xpath>
          <value><pawnsPlural>hunters</pawnsPlural></value>
        </li>

        <!-- "boss" -> Captain. -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="Pirate"]/leaderTitle</xpath>
          <value><leaderTitle>Captain</leaderTitle></value>
        </li>

        <!-- 1 -> 0.6. Four settlements. -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="Pirate"]/settlementGenerationWeight</xpath>
          <value><settlementGenerationWeight>0.6</settlementGenerationWeight></value>
        </li>

        <!--
          ================================================================
          faction_religions_spec.md entry 10 (B54)
          ================================================================
          `ideoName` and `ideoDescription` verbatim; they are the only strings
          the engine renders. ⛔ `hiddenIdeo` MUST STAY UNSET or the
          description is never shown. Structure meme goes FIRST in
          `forcedMemes`.

          `Pirate` ships `requiredMemes` + `structureMemeWeights`, which STEER a
          generated religion. `fixedIdeo` means do not generate, so both are
          dead weight and are removed.
        -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationRemove">
          <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="Pirate"]/requiredMemes</xpath>
        </li>
        <li Class="PatchOperationRemove">
          <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="Pirate"]/structureMemeWeights</xpath>
        </li>
        <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="Pirate"]</xpath>
          <value>
            <fixedIdeo>true</fixedIdeo>
            <requiredPreceptsOnly>false</requiredPreceptsOnly>
            <ideoName>the Contract</ideoName>
            <ideoDescription>A contract is the only honest thing two strangers can hold between them. It names one person, one price, one ending, and everyone not written into it walks away untouched. We do not pillage — pillage is confessing you could not find the one you came for. Take the mark or refuse it in the open. Once it is taken it is finished, or you are.</ideoDescription>
            <forcedMemes>
              <li>Structure_Ideological</li>
              <li MayRequire="vanillaexpanded.vmemese">VME_Bushido</li>
              <li MayRequire="vanillaexpanded.vmemese">VME_Anonymity</li>
              <li>Individualist</li>
              <li>Guilty</li>
            </forcedMemes>
          </value>
        </li>

        <!-- Bespoke world-map icon. the def writes it - Core/Defs/FactionDefs/Factions_Misc.xml:522, so REPLACE. -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="Pirate"]/factionIconPath</xpath>
          <value><factionIconPath>World/JawaFactions/BlackstarCompany</factionIconPath></value>
        </li>

        <!-- The name the world object carries. No vanilla FactionDef writes fixedName
             (checked in Core/Defs/FactionDefs/Factions_Misc.xml), so this is an ADD.
             A Replace would match nothing and log red. factionNameMaker stays: it still
             names this faction's SETTLEMENTS. -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="Pirate"]</xpath>
          <value><fixedName>Blackstar Company</fixedName></value>
        </li>


        <!-- ═══ AUTHORED_KINDS_MUST_FIELD_1 - the Company fields itself ═══════════
             Six Replaces, one per vanilla COMBAT group, keeping each group's own
             tactical character and its commonality. The xpath selects on kindDef AND
             commonality because `Pirate` writes all six on the def itself, so they are
             reachable - unlike TribeCivil, whose groups live on the abstract TribeBase
             and cannot be Replaced on the child at all.
             ⚠️ A Replace that matches nothing logs nothing. If a raid ever arrives as
             vanilla pirates again, suspect a commonality one of these xpaths no longer
             matches, not a weighting. -->

        <!-- commonality 100: the common raid, ranged with melee mix-ins -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="Pirate"]/pawnGroupMakers/li[kindDef="Combat"][commonality="100"]/options</xpath>
          <value>
            <options>
                    <Jawa_Blackstar_Grunt>10</Jawa_Blackstar_Grunt>
                    <Jawa_Blackstar_Heavy>5</Jawa_Blackstar_Heavy>
                    <Jawa_Blackstar_Specialist>3</Jawa_Blackstar_Specialist>
            </options>
          </value>
        </li>

        <!-- commonality 30: close work. Vanilla calls this its melee-only group; the Company has no melee
               role, so its close-quarters shape is carried by the heavy instead -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="Pirate"]/pawnGroupMakers/li[kindDef="Combat"][commonality="30"]/options</xpath>
          <value>
            <options>
                    <Jawa_Blackstar_Heavy>10</Jawa_Blackstar_Heavy>
                    <Jawa_Blackstar_Grunt>5</Jawa_Blackstar_Grunt>
            </options>
          </value>
        </li>

        <!-- commonality 20: ranged only -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="Pirate"]/pawnGroupMakers/li[kindDef="Combat"][commonality="20"]/options</xpath>
          <value>
            <options>
                    <Jawa_Blackstar_Grunt>10</Jawa_Blackstar_Grunt>
                    <Jawa_Blackstar_Specialist>6</Jawa_Blackstar_Specialist>
            </options>
          </value>
        </li>

        <!-- commonality 15: the heavy party. Vanilla's explosives group; the Mandalorian carries it -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="Pirate"]/pawnGroupMakers/li[kindDef="Combat"][commonality="15"]/options</xpath>
          <value>
            <options>
                    <Jawa_Blackstar_Heavy>10</Jawa_Blackstar_Heavy>
                    <Jawa_Blackstar_Grunt>4</Jawa_Blackstar_Grunt>
            </options>
          </value>
        </li>

        <!-- commonality 10: snipers only - the Blackstar hunter is exactly this -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="Pirate"]/pawnGroupMakers/li[kindDef="Combat"][commonality="10"]/options</xpath>
          <value>
            <options>
                    <Jawa_Blackstar_Specialist>10</Jawa_Blackstar_Specialist>
            </options>
          </value>
        </li>

        <!-- commonality 2.5: the rare small party, maxTotalPoints 1000 on the vanilla group -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="Pirate"]/pawnGroupMakers/li[kindDef="Combat"][commonality="2.5"]/options</xpath>
          <value>
            <options>
                    <Jawa_Blackstar_Grunt>10</Jawa_Blackstar_Grunt>
            </options>
          </value>
        </li>

        <!-- The leader is generated once per faction, not rolled into a raid. -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="Pirate"]</xpath>
          <value>
            <fixedLeaderKinds>
              <li>Jawa_Blackstar_Leader</li>
            </fixedLeaderKinds>
          </value>
        </li>

      </operations>
    </match>
  </Operation>

  <!-- ═══ LEADER_TITLES_ON_THE_IDEO_1, 2026-08-22 ═══════════════════════════════
       `Faction.LeaderTitle` (RimWorld/Faction.cs:142) prefers the primary IDEO's
       `leaderTitleMale` and only falls back to `def.leaderTitle`. Measured live:
       the ideo overrode the def on 36 of 37 factions, so Blackstar Company's authored
       title "Captain" was never the word a player read. The ideo's title is
       generated from its CULTURE's `leaderTitleMaker`, so the route is a culture
       of our own - full mechanism in `Defs/CultureDefs/JawaLeaderTitles.xml`.
       ⛔ Not a patch on the shared vanilla culture: Kriminul is shared with every
       faction of its category in 578 mods and patching it renames all of them.
       ⚠️ This BAKES at world creation and cannot be retrofitted. -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="Pirate"]/allowedCultures</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationReplace">
      <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="Pirate"]/allowedCultures</xpath>
      <value><allowedCultures><li>Jawa_Culture_Blackstar</li></allowedCultures></value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
